    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Built from 1406 to 1420, the palace was the ceremonial and political centre of the Chinese government for over 500 years.</li><li>Its layout, colours and numbers were planned to express imperial majesty and the order of heaven and earth.</li><li>Since 1925 it has been the Palace Museum, whose collections grew from the Ming and Qing imperial collections.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A common story says the palace has 9,999 rooms, but survey evidence counts 8,886 bays of rooms in 980 surviving buildings.</p></aside>
    </section>

